# Piet Language Semantics

Reference: https://www.dangermouse.net/esoteric/piet.html

## Stack Underflow
- If an instruction needs values popped and there aren't enough, the instruction is **silently ignored**
- Do NOT throw exceptions or terminate the program on stack underflow

## Modulo
- Result must have the **same sign as the divisor** (top value)
- Use `((a % b) + b) % b` for correct floored modulo

## Roll
- First pop = number of rolls, second pop = depth
- Depth must be >= 0; depth of 0 is a no-op
- **Negative rolls** roll in the opposite direction (do NOT use `Math.Abs`)
- A single positive roll buries the top element `depth` levels deep

## White Codel Sliding
- When entering a white region, slide in the DP direction
- If the slide hits an edge or black block: rotate DP clockwise AND toggle CC
- Retry sliding up to 4 times; if all fail, the program terminates
- This is a **separate** retry mechanism from the normal 8-attempt edge retry

## Program Termination
- Normal termination: 8 failed attempts to leave a non-white color block
- White block termination: 4 failed slide attempts from a white region
- Division/modulo by zero: silently ignore (push operands back)
